#---
# purpose: "a delivered call to Kernel.+, Kernel.-, Kernel.* is the extern inline in the caller, and so is a call to a function that only calls them, so a loop whose body adds, subtracts, multiplies and calls such a function builds no continuation, and the loop spends one reduction per iteration"
# kind: run
#---
#
# `run/2` makes four non-tail calls per iteration: `n - 1`, `P.f(n, 0)`, the
# `+` inside `P.f` and the `*` inside `P.g`. None of the callees can suspend
# the process, so every one is lowered in the loop and the loop builds no
# continuation. The program prints the iteration count, the continuations
# built beyond the ones reduction yields build (one per yield), and the
# reductions spent. The one continuation left is `main`'s own call into the
# loop, which is a call cycle. The interpreter builds no continuations and
# spends no reductions.
defmodule P do
  def f(a, b), do: g(a + b)
  def g(x), do: x * 2 + 1
end

defmodule L do
  def run(0, acc), do: acc
  def run(n, _acc), do: run(n - 1, P.f(n, 0))
end

def main() do
  iterations = 100000
  before = System.alloc_stats()
  result = L.run(iterations, 0)
  after_run = System.alloc_stats()
  dbg(result)
  dbg(after_run[:continuation_allocs] - before[:continuation_allocs] - (after_run[:reduction_yields] - before[:reduction_yields]))
  dbg(after_run[:reductions_executed] - before[:reductions_executed])
end
